# Trackmate — Cursor project intelligence

## Product
- Name is **Trackmate**.
- Dark-first PWA with a light theme toggle (sun/moon switch).
- Local demo works with zero env vars (SQLite). Production is **Vercel + Supabase**.
- Reading **rooms** up to **5** members; creator is **owner** (kick / delete room).

## Architecture rules
- UI reads **only** from `useSessionStore`. Never fetch Supabase from a component.
- Persistence goes through `SyncAdapter` (`local-adapter` | `supabase-adapter`).
- Page turns: optimistic Zustand → `debounceMutex` 420ms → adapter. Persist the **latest** page, not every tap.
- Production auth: Supabase Auth (email/password + **Google OAuth** + reset emails). Google Client ID/Secret live in the Supabase dashboard; the app only calls `signInWithOAuth`. Same Gmail as an existing password user stays one account if automatic linking is on. `git push` does not wipe Supabase Auth.
- Covers: catalog search (Open Library / iTunes / Google Books / **TVMaze** for series) — user **taps to approve**. Manual upload opens a **2:3 crop** (`CoverCropModal`) before save.
- UI names go through `personName()` (`lib/names.ts`). Never show an email local-part on progress bars, people, or notes. `ensureProfile` overwrites handle-like `display_name` with Google `given_name` when present.
- People of a title live on **book/course/movie detail**, not Home. `removeFromTitle` is optimistic (list updates without a refresh).
- Note read receipts: `note_reads` (`0005_note_reads.sql`). Sender sees ticks and can tap for names. Apply `0005` on the existing Supabase project.
- Shelf kinds: `book` | `course` | `movie` | `series` (`0004` + `0006_series.sql`). Progress units are pages / lessons / minutes / episodes. Movie tab has Film | Series.
- **Local demo auth:** salted SHA-256 + HMAC (`pagemate-access-token`) via `/api/auth/*` (returns 501 when Supabase env is set).
- Sign out is confirmed in a modal.
- Do not cache `/api/*` or cross-origin in `public/sw.js`.
- Push send lives in `app/api/push/send/route.ts` (Node runtime). Fans out to **people who can open that title** via service role when Supabase is configured. Dead 404/410 endpoints are pruned. The client **heals** the subscription on focus (browsers often rotate endpoints without firing `pushsubscriptionchange`).
- Settings: **Check for updates** (`usePWAUpdate.checkNow`) + **Report a bug** (`BUG_REPORT_EMAIL`). iOS Web Push requires Home Screen / standalone + **HTTPS**.
- Shelf search (`lib/search.ts`) matches title, creator, and kind (book / course / movie / series).

## Rooms & invites
- Primary invite: **Share this book** → `/join/{code}?book={id}` grants **that book only** (`shelf_scope=books` + `book_access`).
- Secondary: room invite `/join/{code}` with warning that the **whole shelf** is shared (`shelf_scope=all`).
- Never share account passwords. No read-only role in v1.
- New rooms start with an **empty shelf** (no sample seed book).
- Schema: `reading_rooms` + `room_members` (`0002_rooms.sql`); book scope + covers bucket (`0003_book_access.sql`); title kinds (`0004_title_kinds.sql`).

## Design
- Colors: canvas `#0F172A`, brand `#6366F1`, accent `#F59E0B`, cream `#F5F0E8`.
- Settings: GitHub / MIT open source. Buy Me a Coffee is commented out.
- Logo: `components/branding/TrackmateLogo.tsx`.
- Fonts: Outfit + Fraunces + Vazirmatn via `next/font/local` from `app/fonts`. `adjustFontFallback: false`. Re-fetch with `node scripts/fetch-fonts.mjs`.
- Theme: `useThemeStore` + `ThemeSwitch`. Persist `pagemate-theme`. Settings → Appearance only.
- Bottom nav + `env(safe-area-inset-bottom)`. Touch targets ≥ 44px.
- Glass: `.glass` / `.glass-strong` in `app/globals.css`. Light theme on `html.light`.

## Docs
When changing debounce, RLS, SW, rooms, or push, update `docs/ARCHITECTURE_AND_IMPLEMENTATION.md` and `docs/VERCEL_DEPLOY.md` as needed.
